00:29:15,440 --> 00:29:16,690
或膜世界中
or brane world.

531
00:29:16,810 --> 00:29:18,530
其他的膜世界
The other brane world,

532
00:29:18,640 --> 00:29:21,900
尽管很靠近我们
even though it's incredibly close to us,

533
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:25,900
并且是一个不影响我们的独立的宇宙
is a separate universe that does not interact with us.

534
00:29:26,010 --> 00:29:30,140
但是Paul开始怀疑它如果影响我们会发生什么
But then Paul began to wonder what would happen if it did.

535
00:29:30,250 --> 00:29:32,910
Steinhardt：我的同事和我 开始考虑的是这样一种想法——
What my colleagues and l began to think about

536
00:29:33,020 --> 00:29:35,880
这些膜世界可能不是永远
was the idea that these brane worlds might not just sit there

537
00:29:35,990 --> 00:29:37,180
处于那里
for all time,

538
00:29:37,290 --> 00:29:39,080
它们可能开始向着彼此移动
that they might begin to move towards one another

539
00:29:39,190 --> 00:29:40,650
并真地碰撞起来
and actually collide.

540
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:42,050
在碰撞过程中
ln that collision,

