576
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:30,160
发生的事情好像是在黑洞形成的那个点上
What happens is as if you've pinned the two together

577
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:32,860
把两个膜钉到一起
at that point where the black hole forms.

578
00:31:32,970 --> 00:31:36,000
所以在别处，这两个膜可能是分离的
So elsewhere, the two branes may be separate,

579
00:31:36,110 --> 00:31:38,730
只是在被钉在一起的那个点上
but at the point where they're pinned,

580
00:31:38,850 --> 00:31:41,100
在黑洞的位置上它们结合在一起
they're joined together at the position of the black hole.

581
00:31:41,220 --> 00:31:43,540
弗里曼：解码暗物质之谜
Decoding the riddle of dark matter

582
00:31:43,650 --> 00:31:46,980
在今天的物理学上是最大的挑战之一
is one of the biggest challenges in physics today.

583
00:31:47,090 --> 00:31:48,880
成千上万个精明的头脑
Thousands of brilliant minds

584
00:31:48,990 --> 00:31:51,410
以及成百上千个望远镜为它准备
and hundreds of telescopes are trained on it.

585
00:31:51,530 --> 00:31:53,580
Paul相信当他们最终了解了
Paul believes that when they finally learn

586
00:31:53,700 --> 00:31:55,020
暗物质是什么
what dark matter is,

587
00:31:55,130 --> 00:32:00,790
他们会发现暗物质存在于别的宇宙中
they will actually discover that it exists in another universe.

588
00:32:00,900 --> 00:32:04,460
黑洞把我们和平行宇宙联系起来了吗？
Do black holes connect us to a parallel world?

589
00:32:04,570 --> 00:32:07,900
有位科学家可能已经有答案了
This scientist may already have the answer,

590
00:32:08,010 --> 00:32:10,700
并且如果他的新理论是正确的
and if his new theory is correct,

591
00:32:10,810 --> 00:32:13,370
那么我们可能在与平行宇宙
we could be on the verge of making contact

592
00:32:13,480 --> 00:32:15,970
接触的边缘
with a parallel universe.

593
00:32:18,420 --> 00:32:20,810
400年前
400 years ago,

594
00:32:20,920 --> 00:32:25,410
地球被认为是宇宙的中心
it was believed Earth was the center of the Universe.

595
00:32:25,780 --> 00:32:29,510
后来一个来自波兰托伦市乡村的人
Then a man from the village Torun in Poland

596
00:32:29,620 --> 00:32:31,510
排除了地球
swept the Earth aside.

597
00:32:31,620 --> 00:32:34,910
但是在探索我们在宇宙中的真实位置的过程中
But in discovering our true place in the cosmos,

598
00:32:35,020 --> 00:32:37,850
伟大的天文学家尼古拉·哥白尼
the great astronomer Nicolas Copernicus

599
