留下一个至关重要的问题没有解答
left one crucial question unanswered.

600
00:32:40,700 --> 00:32:44,390
宇宙的中心在哪？
Where is the center of the Universe?

601
00:32:44,500 --> 00:32:47,360
现在，同一个乡村的另一个男孩
Now another son of that same village

602
00:32:47,470 --> 00:32:49,330
认为他有答案
thinks he has the answer.

603
00:32:49,440 --> 00:32:54,530
如果他是对的，那么答案将指引我们找到平行宇宙
lf he's right, it could lead us to a parallel universe,

604
00:32:54,640 --> 00:32:57,930
给了我们宇宙起源的平行宇宙
one that gave birth to ours.

605
00:32:58,050 --> 00:33:02,240
Nikodem Poplawski有着同样的创新精神
Nikodem Poplawski has the same revolutionary spirit

606
00:33:02,350 --> 00:33:04,440
就像他的波兰前辈一样
as his Polish predecessor.

607
00:33:04,550 --> 00:33:08,040
他相信科学突破的关键
He believes the key to making a scientific breakthrough

608
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:12,250
是严格的训练和一个清晰的头脑
is rigorous training and a clear head.

609
00:33:12,360 --> 00:33:15,990
Poplawski：当我解决问题时，我精神饱满
When l work out, l have some freshness in my mind,

610
00:33:16,100 --> 00:33:18,820
接下来我想一些
and then l want to think about some problems

611
00:33:18,930 --> 00:33:20,090
关于宇宙的问题
about the Universe.

612
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,640
我变得更有创意
l become more creative.

613
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:26,560
弗里曼：Nikodem强烈的关注使直接面对
Nikodem's intense focus brought him face-to-face

614
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:28,000
宇宙怪物——
with a cosmic monster --

615
00:33:28,110 --> 00:33:30,670
黑洞
the black hole.

616
00:33:30,780 --> 00:33:34,900
在其外缘，被称为视界
lnside its outer edge, known as the event horizon,

617
00:33:35,020 --> 00:33:38,070
甚至连光也无法逃脱它贪婪的胃口
not even light can escape its voracious appetite.

618
00:33:38,190 --> 00:33:42,080
没有人知道 穿过这个没有归路的宇宙点会发生什么
No one is sure what happens past this cosmic point of no return.

619
00:33:42,190 --> 00:33:43,950
在黑洞的中心
At the heart of a black hole,

620
00:33:44,060 --> 00:33:46,380
引力的力量是如此强大的
the force of gravity is so powerful

621
00:33:46,500 --> 00:33:49,490
以至于它会把恒星的全部质量
that it will compress the entire mass of a star

622
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:52,450
压缩成一个单点
into a single point.

623
00:33:52,570 --> 00:33:58,230
物理学家把这一密度无穷大的点称为奇点
Physicists call this point of infinite density a singularity.

624
00:33:58,340 --> 00:34:00,300
Poplawski：当然，奇点意味着
And, of course, singularity means

625
00:34:00,410 --> 00:34:02,530
我们不完全了解这种物理现象
that we do not understand completely the physics.

626
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:06,570
我不喜欢奇点
l don't like singularities,

627
00:34:06,680 --> 00:34:10,010
并且我想看看是否有一种结构
and l wanted to see if there is a mechanism

628
00:34:10,120 --> 00:34:13,810
是最简单的和最自然的
which would be the simplest and the most natural.

629
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:18,280
弗里曼：像大部分研究引力的科学家一样
Like most scientists who study gravity,

630
00:34:18,390 --> 00:34:23,090
Nikodem是一个阿尔伯特·爱因斯坦的追随者
Nikodem is a disciple of Albert Einstein.

631
00:34:23,200 --> 00:34:27,590
爱因斯坦声称 空间和时间交织在一起
Einstein professed that space and time are woven together

632
00:34:27,700 --> 00:34:31,190
成为一种柔性织物，他称之为时空的
into a flexible fabric he called space-time.

633
00:34:31,310 --> 00:34:35,060
Katie和Meghan正拿着一块毛巾过来
Katie and Meghan are holding here a towel,

634
00:34:35,180 --> 00:34:37,400
代表时空
which represents space-time.

635
00:34:37,510 --> 00:34:39,500
时空在大质量物体的影响下
Space-time can be curved

636
00:34:39,610 --> 00:34:43,010
可以弯曲
under the influence of massive objects.

637
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:46,580
我这里有球，它代表着太阳
So here l have the ball, which represents the sun.

638
00:34:46,690 --> 00:34:52,150
太阳对时空有很显著的影响
Sun has some significant effect on the space-time.

639
00:34:52,260 --> 00:34:55,780
你可以看到时空是如何弯曲的
You can see how space-time is curved.

640
00:34:55,900 --> 00:34:57,520
这是地球
And here's Earth.

641
00:34:57,630 --> 00:35:00,520
而且地球感觉到时空的弯曲
And Earth feels curvature of space-time,

642
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:03,030
这就是为什么它围绕太阳转动
and that's why it moves around the sun.

643
00:35:03,140 --> 00:35:06,660
弗里曼：但这条曲线不是唯一的路径
But this curving was not the only way

644
00:35:06,780 --> 00:35:09,770
爱因斯坦认为物质会扭曲
Einstein believed matter could distort

645
00:35:09,880 --> 00:35:11,770
时空结构
the fabric of space-time.

646
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:13,400
除弯曲之外
ln addition to curvature,

647
00:35:13,520 --> 00:35:16,910
时空还具有另一个几何特性
space-time is also equipped with another geomatical property

648
00:35:17,020 --> 00:35:18,210
叫做扭曲
called torsion.

649
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:21,740
弗里曼：阿尔伯特·爱因斯坦 以及数学家Elie Cartan
Albert Einstein and mathematician Elie Cartan

650
00:35:21,860 --> 00:35:25,080
相信在时空结构中物质
believed matter could also twist individual fibers

651
00:35:25,190 --> 00:35:27,180
也能扭成特别的纤维
in the fabric of space-time.

652
00:35:27,300 --> 00:35:30,520
然而，扭曲的效果是如此地小
However, the effects of torsion are so tiny,

653
00:35:30,630 --> 00:35:32,790
它们是无法测量的
they are impossible to measure.

654
00:35:32,900 --> 00:35:34,960
没有任何手段来测试它
Without any means to test it,

655
00:35:35,070 --> 00:35:38,630
爱因斯坦和Cartan放弃了这一理论
Einstein and Cartan abandoned the theory.

656
00:35:38,740 --> 00:35:41,460
但Nikodem在他们停下的地方拾起这一理论
But Nikodem picked up where they left off.

657
00:35:41,580 --> 00:35:43,030
他把他的理论运用到
He applied their theory

658
00:35:43,150 --> 00:35:46,170
黑洞中的无情的引力上
to the unforgiving gravity inside a black hole,

659
00:35:46,280 --> 00:35:48,800
在黑洞中物质飞速旋转
where matter spins so fast,

660
00:35:48,920 --> 00:35:53,410
扭曲把时空扭成一个螺旋弹簧
torsion twists space-time into a coiled spring,

661
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:55,890
等待爆发
waiting to explode.

662
00:36:00,900 --> 00:36:03,690
这是即将崩塌的黑洞
So, here is the collapsing black hole.

663
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:07,390
在一个管子中的龙卷风 可见到
Tornado in a tube visualize the very violent dynamics

664
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:11,130
物质通过视界时的非常剧烈的动力学
of the motion of the matter through the event horizon.

665
00:36:11,240 --> 00:36:13,360
在极高的密度下
At extremely high densities,

666
00:36:13,480 --> 00:36:17,200
扭曲开始变得明显
torsion starts becoming significant

667
00:36:17,310 --> 00:36:19,700
而表现为一种力量
and manifests itself as a force

668
00:36:19,820 --> 00:36:23,010
与万有引力对立
that opposes gravitational attraction.

669
00:36:23,120 --> 00:36:26,940
弗里曼：当物质接近黑洞中心时
As matter approaches the heart of a black hole,

670
00:36:27,060 --> 00:36:28,840
扭曲变得如此极端
torsion becomes so extreme

671
00:36:28,960 --> 00:36:32,110
以至于它用强大的力量使周围的物质四处旋转
that it spins the matter around with intense force.

672
00:36:32,230 --> 00:36:34,920
物质没有坍塌为奇点
Matter does not fall into a singular point.

673
00:36:35,030 --> 00:36:40,560
反而，黑洞的中心是漩涡口
lnstead, the heart of a black hole is a swirling opening.

674
00:36:40,670 --> 00:36:43,360
Poplawski：物质恰恰不会消失
The matter cannot just disappear.

675
00:36:43,470 --> 00:36:45,160
能量一定是守恒的
The energy must be conserved.

676
00:36:45,270 --> 00:36:48,200
所以所有的物质穿过视界
So all the matter goes through the event horizon

677
00:36:48,310 --> 00:36:51,900
从一个黑洞到另一边的成长中的白洞
from a black hole to the growing white hole on the other side

678
00:36:52,010 --> 00:36:56,710
参与创建新成长的宇宙
and participates in creating new growing universe.

679
00:36:56,820 --> 00:36:58,910
弗里曼：如果Nikodem是对的
lf Nikodem is right,

680
00:36:59,020 --> 00:37:02,850
当恒星的质量塌陷成一个黑洞时
when the mass of a star collapses into a black hole,

681
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:07,620
它在另一边喷涌出一个白洞
it spews out on the other side as a white hole,

682
00:37:07,730 --> 00:37:11,320
一个易爆的质量和能量源
an explosive fountain of mass and energy

683
00:37:11,430 --> 00:37:13,720
在新的平行宇宙中
in a new parallel universe.

684
00:37:13,840 --> 00:37:16,330
但这个想法不只是适用于
But this idea does not just apply

685
00:37:16,440 --> 00:37:18,530
我们宇宙中的黑洞
to black holes in our Universe.

686
00:37:18,640 --> 00:37:21,330
如果我们假设每一个黑洞的内部
lf we assume that every black hole

687
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:23,670
都产生一个新宇宙
produces a new universe inside,

688
00:37:23,780 --> 00:37:28,670
那么我们的宇宙一定诞生于
then our Universe must have been born in a black hole

689
00:37:28,780 --> 00:37:31,940
另一个宇宙中的黑洞
which exists in another universe.

690
00:37:32,050 --> 00:37:35,940
弗里曼：Nikodem相信创造我们宇宙的大爆炸
Nikodem believes the Big Bang that created our Universe

691
00:37:36,060 --> 00:37:37,510
实际上是一个白洞
was actually a white hole

692
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:42,320
由另一个宇宙的死亡的恒星创造
created in turn by the death of a star in another cosmos,

693
00:37:42,430 --> 00:37:44,720
那个宇宙是我们的母亲
a cosmos that is our parent.

694
00:37:44,830 --> 00:37:47,190
如果这一理论是正确的
And if this theory is correct,

695
00:37:47,300 --> 00:37:50,590
这两个世界之间
there should be a cosmic umbilical cord

696
00:37:50,710 --> 00:37:52,730
应该有一个
between these two worlds,

697
00:37:52,840 --> 00:37:55,260
从来没有被切断的宇宙脐带
one that has never been severed.

698
00:37:55,380 --> 00:37:58,770
Poplawski：如果我们在一个黑洞内
lf we are inside a black hole,

699
00:37:58,880 --> 00:38:01,540
那么一定有一个
then there must be a connection

700
00:38:01,650 --> 00:38:04,440
从母宇宙到我们的宇宙的联系
from the parent universe to our Universe.

701
00:38:04,550 --> 00:38:10,980
弗里曼：这位科学家 偶然发现通向另一个宇宙的桥梁了吗？
Has this scientist stumbled upon a bridge to another universe?

702
00:38:11,090 --> 00:38:13,980
在夜晚的天空中奇怪的能量爆发
And could strange bursts of energy in the night sky

703
00:38:14,100 --> 00:38:16,990
实际上会是完全出乎意料的东西吗？
actually be something totally unexpected...

704
00:38:17,100 --> 00:38:21,300
来自于平行宇宙的居民的消息？
messages from the inhabitants of a parallel universe?

705
00:38:23,200 --> 00:38:28,460
黑洞是宇宙中最可怕的东西
Black holes are the most terrifying things in the Universe.

706
00:38:28,570 --> 00:38:33,500
掉落其中的任何事物会永远消失
Anything that falls into one is gone forever.

707
00:38:34,070 --> 00:38:38,230
但事物去了哪里了呢？
But where does it go?

708
00:38:38,340 --> 00:38:41,600
答案可能是另一个宇宙
The answer could be another universe.

709
00:38:41,710 --> 00:38:43,600
如果这个想法是正确的
lf this idea is right,

710
00:38:43,720 --> 00:38:47,470
黑洞可能是一种把消息发送到
black holes might be a way to send a message

711
00:38:47,590 --> 00:38:49,310
平行宇宙的方式
to a parallel world.

712
00:38:49,420 --> 00:38:52,310
并且还有另一种可能性
And there's another possibility.

713
00:38:52,420 --> 00:38:55,210
来自另一个宇宙的人
Beings from another universe

714
00:38:55,330 --> 00:39:00,150
可能已经尝试过与我们联系
may already have tried to make contact with us.

715
00:39:00,270 --> 00:39:03,290
物理学家Nikodem Poplawski相信
Physicist Nikodem Poplawski is convinced

716
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:07,260
我们的宇宙静止在
that our Universe rests at the bottom of a black hole

717
00:39:07,370 --> 00:39:09,230
平行世界的黑洞的末端
in a parallel world.

718
00:39:09,340 --> 00:39:11,800
并且他正试图探索
And he's trying to discover

719
00:39:11,910 --> 00:39:15,430
在那个平行世界中人们是否
whether beings in that parallel world

720
00:39:15,550 --> 00:39:19,570
可能有一种方法与我们联系
might have a way to communicate with us.

721
00:39:22,050 --> 00:39:23,510
想象一下
And this is a visualization

722
00:39:23,620 --> 00:39:25,880
当物质和能量走向黑洞时
of what happens to the matter and energy

723
00:39:25,990 --> 00:39:27,980
会发生什么
when it goes to a black hole.

724
00:39:28,090 --> 00:39:32,290
弗里曼：黑洞里面的引力是很强烈的
The gravity inside a black hole is so intense,

725
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:34,190
如果你跳进一个黑洞
if you jumped into one,

726
00:39:34,300 --> 00:39:37,360
它会撕裂你身体里的每个原子
it would rip apart every atom in your body.

727
00:39:37,470 --> 00:39:43,230
但这并不意味着没有东西可以生存之旅
But that doesn't mean nothing can survive the trip.

728
00:39:43,340 --> 00:39:48,070
现在我要用波兰语写下“时空”这个词
Now l'm going to write the word "Space-time" in Polish,

729
00:39:48,180 --> 00:39:52,410
“Czasoprzesetrzen”
"Czasoprzesetrzen."

730
00:39:52,520 --> 00:39:54,210
现在我要把它撕下
Now l'm going to rip it off,

731
00:39:54,320 --> 00:39:59,280
并把这一小张纸放到搅拌机中
and l'm going to put little piece of paper to the blender.

732
00:39:59,390 --> 00:40:03,420
接着我要按下按钮
And l'm going to press the button.

733
00:40:03,530 --> 00:40:07,090
无论我想要按住按钮多久
No matter how long l'm going to press the button,

734
00:40:07,200 --> 00:40:09,390
信息仍然存在
the information is still there.

735
00:40:09,500 --> 00:40:11,760
现在信息完全失真
Now it's very distorted.

736
00:40:11,870 --> 00:40:14,630
我们不能轻易地识别出
We cannot easily recognize it.

737
00:40:14,740 --> 00:40:17,000
然而，它在黑洞中
However, it is inside a black hole,

738
00:40:17,110 --> 00:40:20,670
它会出现在另外一面，在白洞内
and it will appear on the other side inside the white hole,

739
00:40:20,780 --> 00:40:22,870
并且我们希望有一天
and we can hope that one day

740
00:40:22,980 --> 00:40:26,810
有人能解读这条信息
someone will be able to decipher this information.

741
00:40:26,920 --> 00:40:31,240
弗里曼：我们的宇宙母亲可能 正在给我们发送信息吗？
Could our cosmic parents be sending us messages?

742
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:34,950
Nikodem认为我们可能已经已经发现了
Nikodem thinks we may already have detected evidence

743
00:40:35,060 --> 00:40:36,080
她们发信息的证据
that they are.

744
00:40:36,200 --> 00:40:38,520
几十年来，天文学家们获得
For decades, astronomers have picked up

745
00:40:38,630 --> 00:40:40,020
来自宇宙遥远区域的
powerful bursts of energy

746
00:40:40,130 --> 00:40:44,690
巨大能量爆发
coming from the farthest reaches of the cosmos.

747
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:48,460
Poplawski：伽玛射线爆发是除宇宙大爆炸以外
Gamma-ray bursts are the most luminous explosions

748
00:40:48,570 --> 00:40:53,500
我们在我们的宇宙中观察到的最强的爆炸
that we observe in our Universe besides the Big Bang.

749
00:40:53,610 --> 00:40:57,100
并且我们仍然不是很了解
And we still do not understand well

750
00:40:57,220 --> 00:41:02,780
形成它们的机理
the mechanism that causes them.

751
00:41:02,890 --> 00:41:05,980
我们看到它们从遥远遥远的地方来了
We see them coming from far, far away.

752
00:41:06,090 --> 00:41:08,850
他们可能是从母宇宙来到我们宇宙的
They may be indications of matter

753
00:41:08,960 --> 00:41:12,720
物质的象征
coming from the parent universe to our Universe.

754
00:41:12,830 --> 00:41:17,220
弗里曼：这些能量脉冲实际上 会是一种莫尔斯电码形式吗？
Could these pulses of energy actually be a form of Morse Code

755
00:41:17,340 --> 00:41:20,330
来自于另一个宇宙的居民
from inhabitants of another universe,

756
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:23,300
一个意义深刻的宇宙智慧的消息
a message of profound cosmic wisdom

757
00:41:23,410 --> 00:41:26,770
基于数十亿年的经验
based on billions of years of experience

758
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:29,840
在我们的宇宙诞生以前？
before our Universe was even born?

759
00:41:29,950 --> 00:41:33,270
Nikodem的理论还在初期
Nikodem's theory is still young,

760
00:41:33,390 --> 00:41:36,410
并且数学史令人畏惧的
and the math is intimidating.

761
00:41:36,520 --> 00:41:39,350
他可能是错的
He could be wrong.

762
00:41:39,460 --> 00:41:41,650
但在他的扭转平行宇宙的奋争过程中
But in his struggle to wrench parallel universes

763
00:41:41,760 --> 00:41:44,080
从空想的领域
from the realm of fantasy

764
00:41:44,200 --> 00:41:47,620
变成一个严肃的科学可能的领域
to one of serious scientific possibility,

765
00:41:47,730 --> 00:41:50,620
他并不孤独
he is far from alone.

766
00:41:50,740 --> 00:41:53,890
一旦你细想整个多元宇宙这一观点
Once you consider the full multiverse point of view,

767
00:41:54,010 --> 00:41:56,460
你看到一个更广泛的现实描绘
you see a much broader picture of reality.

768
00:41:56,580 --> 00:41:59,430
Tegmark：每当两个不同的事情发生
Whenever two different things happen,

769
00:41:59,550 --> 00:42:01,700
你只会察觉到其中的一个
you would just be aware of one of them.

770
00:42:01,810 --> 00:42:05,140
你会错误地认为没有发生其他的结果
You would think mistakenly that the other outcome didn't happen,

771
00:42:05,250 --> 00:42:07,770
但实际上，你的另一个副本
but in fact, the other copy of you

772
00:42:07,890 --> 00:42:10,610
会感觉其他方式
would feel just the other way around.

773
00:42:10,720 --> 00:42:12,710
我们开始讨论
We start discussing things

774
00:42:12,830 --> 00:42:17,020
以前属于科幻小说的领域的东西
which previously belonged to realm of science fiction.

775
00:42:17,130 --> 00:42:20,650
我们现在正在非常，非常认真地思考
We are right now thinking about this very, very seriously,

776
00:42:20,770 --> 00:42:24,490
而且也许最终我们会找到一些答案
and maybe eventually we will find some answers.

777
00:42:24,600 --> 00:42:31,160
“宇宙”这个词被认为意味着存在的任何事物
The word "Universe" is supposed to mean everything that exists.

778
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:33,170
今天，我们几乎确定
Today, we're almost certain

779
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:36,140
我们的宇宙不是所有的都有
that our Universe is not all there is.

780
00:42:36,250 --> 00:42:39,710
可能真的有平行地球
There really could be parallel Earths,

781
00:42:39,820 --> 00:42:43,940
平行你，平行我
parallel you's, and parallel me's.

782
00:42:44,060 --> 00:42:48,280
很难不去怀疑其他我可能像什么
lt's hard not to wonder what our alter egos might be like,

783
00:42:48,390 --> 00:42:52,350
是否他们正过着我们最钟爱的梦想的生活
whether they are living out our most cherished dreams.

784
00:42:52,460 --> 00:42:55,490
但不要忘了这种可能性——
But don't forget this possibility --

785
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:59,630
你可能已经生活在
you could already be living the dream

786
00:42:59,740 --> 00:43:03,270
来自平行宇宙的其他你的梦想中
of another you from a parallel universe.

787
00:43:03,570 --> 00:43:04,570
-- 感谢观赏 --

